course: dictionary
lesson: 774
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. To find the right one, read the words around it. «The lion is the king of the beasts.» Here a beast is a large, wild animal, because a lion is an animal.
explain: «That maths test was a beast!» Is a test an animal? No. Here beast means something very big, powerful or difficult. Ask yourself: would the animal meaning fit? If not, try another meaning and check it still makes sense in the sentence.
explain: Beast can also be praise in sport slang. «He's a beast at football» means he is amazingly good at it. Phrases have their own meanings too: a beast of burden is an animal that carries loads.
fact: A beast is a large, wild or frightening animal.
fact: A beast can also be a cruel or nasty person, as in «a mean beast».
fact: Informal use: «That maths test was a beast» means it was very difficult.
fact: Slang use: someone who is a beast at something is amazingly good at it.
fact: «Beast of burden» means an animal that carries loads.
exercise: What does beast mean in «the king of the beasts»? | A beast of burden | A nasty person | *Large, wild animals | A very difficult test
exercise: Mia says, «That maths test was a beast!» What does she mean? | A large, wild animal | A cruel person | *Something very difficult | An animal that carries loads
exercise: «He's a beast at football.» What does this mean? | He has fur all over | *He is amazingly good at it | He is cruel to the other players | He carries heavy loads
test: The Rat says the other animals call him «a mean beast». What does beast mean here? | A large, wild animal | An amazingly good player | *A cruel or nasty person | Something very difficult
test: What does «beast of burden» mean? | *An animal that carries loads | A person who is very cruel | A very difficult job | A beast from a fairy tale
exam: In «Beauty and the Beast», which meaning of beast is used? | A cruel or nasty person | *A large, frightening animal | Someone amazingly good at something | Something very difficult
